.TH P3M-DIFF 1 "@DATE@" "p3m @VERSION@" "p3m Manual"
.SH NAME
p3m-diff \- parallel directory comparison
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B p3m-diff
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.I LEFT
.I RIGHT
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B p3m-diff
compares two directory trees in lockstep with a pool of worker threads and
reports the likelihood that their contents are the same.
By default entry names, types, sizes and metadata (mode, owner, group and
mtime at nanosecond precision) are compared.
Every difference is streamed as CSV and summarised at the end with a
plain-language verdict.
.PP
With
.B \-c
file contents are compared too.
The comparison is byte-exact rather than checksum-based: both files are read
in 1\ MiB chunks and compared directly, stopping at (and reporting) the first
differing byte.
A file's size is checked first and the content read is skipped when the sizes
already differ.
.PP
Symbolic links are never followed; they are compared by target, owner and
group and never descended into.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-checksum
Also compare file contents, byte for byte.
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-threads " \fIN\fR"
Worker threads (default: the number of online CPUs).
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " \fIFILE\fR"
Write the CSV listing to
.I FILE
and show a live progress display.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Suppress the console listing; progress and the summary verdict are still
shown.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the version and exit.
.SH OUTPUT
CSV columns:
.IR path ,
.IR difference ,
.IR left ,
.IR right .
.I path
is relative to the roots;
.I difference
is one of
.BR only\-left ,
.BR only\-right ,
.BR type ,
.BR size ,
.BR content ,
.BR mode ,
.BR owner ,
.BR group ,
.BR mtime ,
.BR target ,
.BR device .
.PP
The verdict is one of: very likely identical (default mode), identical
verified byte-for-byte
.RB ( \-c ),
trees differ, or withheld when errors made coverage incomplete.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
No differences.
.TP
.B 1
Differences found.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error, or comparison errors (verdict withheld).
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
p3m\-diff /data/primary /data/replica
p3m\-diff \-c \-j 16 /srv/site /backup/site
p3m\-diff \-q \-o differences.csv /a /b
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR p3m (7),
.BR p3m\-cp (1),
.BR diff (1),
.BR rsync (1)
